246
00:21:36,340 --> 00:21:39,516
I knew if I left you alone,
you'd turn into a crybaby.

247
00:21:40,420 --> 00:21:43,640
I know you pretty well,
if I do say so myself.

248
00:22:12,380 --> 00:22:16,240
When we get back home, I bet
Alice will be so angry with us.

249
00:22:17,780 --> 00:22:20,980
Maybe not, as long as
we still remember her.

250
00:22:21,580 --> 00:22:23,460
And the time we spent with her.

251
00:22:23,860 --> 00:22:25,978
If we don't forget that, we're good.

252
00:22:26,840 --> 00:22:27,670
Yeah.

253
00:22:28,260 --> 00:22:29,960
We won't forget Alice.

254
00:22:30,600 --> 00:22:31,640
Or Liz.

255
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:32,840
Or Klein.

256
00:22:33,300 --> 00:22:34,860
Or Aikiel and Silica.

257
00:22:35,280 --> 00:22:37,180
Or our little Yui.

258
00:22:38,320 --> 00:22:41,026
As long as we remember
them, we'll be alright.

259
00:22:41,520 --> 00:22:42,350
Won't we?

260
00:22:49,060 --> 00:22:51,917
So how long will we be living here again?

261
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:56,017
About 200 years give or take.

262
00:22:56,100 --> 00:22:58,397
I could do a thousand years!

263
00:22:58,480 --> 00:23:00,657
Easy if I'm with you.

264
00:23:00,740 --> 00:23:04,237
All righty then, let's go.

265
00:23:04,320 --> 00:23:08,300
Yeah, let's get going.

266
00:23:10,140 --> 00:23:13,060
It's a new world now,
and we've got lots to do.

267
00:23:13,740 --> 00:23:15,622
Let's see if we can help it out.

268
00:23:38,720 --> 00:23:40,160
Thank you.
